[00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.080]   Good morning, good afternoon, everyone,
[00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.040]   and thank you for your interest in Constellium.
[00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.440]   Let's turn to slide five.
[00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.800]   At Constellium, the health and safety of our employees is our first priority.
[00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:25.280]   We have implemented many initiatives to protect our employees in response to the COVID-19 pandemic.
[00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:33.120]   We have provided our personnel with personal protective equipment, increased cleaning and sanitation,
[00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:39.960]   allowed for and enforced social distancing, and worked to raise awareness with our employees.
[00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:47.520]   I want to personally thank our employees for taking this seriously and following the precautions we have put into place.
[00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:54.560]   As of last Friday, approximately one-half of 1% of our employees have tested positive for COVID-19.
[00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.080]   And all of whom have recovered or are recovering.
[00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.680]   Needless to say, we must remain vigilant.
[00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.160]   During the second quarter, our plants operated well,
[00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:15.000]   despite the significant disruptions to customer demand from lockdowns in both Europe and the US.
[00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.840]   As I'm speaking, all our plants are running now and well.
[00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.840]   We are carefully monitoring COVID-19 hotspots, both for the health of our employees,
[00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.160]   and any potential impacts on supply chains.
[00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.960]   The demand for our products gradually increased during the course of the second quarter.
[00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.240]   And this trend has continued into July.
[00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:45.920]   However, both levels of demand and visibility from our customers remain below historical levels.
[00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.120]   We took strong actions to combat the effects of the pandemic on our business.
[00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.120]   We aggressively reduced our costs,
[00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.680]   including flexing variable costs to match production levels,
[00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.800]   reducing fixed costs,
[00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.400]   and lowering our targeted capital expenditures.
[00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:11.840]   Over 40% of our workforce were on some type of partial unemployment or temporary layoff scheme during the quarter.
[00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:17.680]   Where appropriate, we have also implemented permanent headcount reduction.
[00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.400]   Our ability to flex costs was slightly better than the scenario we provided last quarter.
[00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:31.480]   This was a great achievement by the entire Constellium team and demonstrated our flexibility and resilience.
[00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:36.480]   Our liquidity at the end of the quarter was €949 million,
[00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.480]   an increase of over €300 million compared to the end of the first quarter.
[00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:51.400]   We added an additional €50 million of liquidity in July through credit facilities supported by the German state,
[00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.400]   bringing our pro-forma liquidity to approximately €1 billion.
[00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.800]   In June, we accessed the debt market to refinance our 2021 bonds.
[00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:09.200]   This transaction removed our only near-term bond maturity at a very attractive coupon.
[00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.960]   In conclusion, with the significant actions we have taken,
[00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:19.560]   I am very confident in our ability to navigate through this crisis.
[00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.680]   On flight six, you will see some of the best results of the last quarter.
[00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.800]   You will see some of our highlights from the second quarter of 2020.
[00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:34.080]   Shipments were 310,000 metric tonnes, a decrease of 25% compared to the second quarter of 2019.
[00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.560]   Revenue decreased 33% to €1 billion.
[00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:44.680]   Of the roughly €500 million decline in revenue compared to the second quarter of last year,
[00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.960]   two-thirds was related to lower shipments and one-third was related to lower metal prices.
[00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:56.960]   I remind you that while our revenues are affected by changes in metal prices,
[00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.440]   we operate a pass-through business model to minimize metal risk.
[00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:11.440]   Net loss of €32 million compared to net income of €17 million in the second quarter of 2019.
[00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:19.240]   Adjusted EBITDA of €81 million decreased 51% compared to the second quarter of 2019,
[00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:29.720]   with a strong focus on cost control, we are able to offset a significant part of the volume headwinds to adjusted EBITDA across each of our business units.
[00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:35.400]   I am proud of what the team was able to achieve in a challenging environment.
[00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.000]   Custodium generated €228 million of adjusted EBITDA in the first half,
